      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The town’s mineral waters attracted Hollywood stars in the 1940s, earning it the title “Spa Capital of the World” with over 120 spas.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://dhshistoricalsociety.org/history-of-dhs/",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Mission Creek Fault, a branch of the San Andreas, separates a hot aquifer from a cold one beneath the city.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://dhshistoricalsociety.org/history-of-dhs/",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Cabot’s Pueblo Museum, a hand‑built adobe structure, is one of Riverside County’s oldest adobe‑style buildings and is listed on the National Register of Historic Places.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10,
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
